WEBVTT

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:07.970
Over there?

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:19.750
I sure didn't think I'd 
end up showing you this.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:25.120
Nightingale Mode.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:04.600
Nightingale Mode?

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.690
S-Somebody...

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.900
H-Help me!

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.910
Miss Florence Nightingale.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:46.710
I'm sorry. I thought we were 
going to have tea.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.460
I didn't come for tea.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.340
I came for your power.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:59.100
Power? You mean that voice?

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:00.370
Correct.

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:06.370
I heard it in 1853,

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:09.650
when I was still just 34 years old.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:16.900
A voice said to save the people 
suffering in the Crimean War,

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.840
so I obeyed and went 
to the front as a nurse.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:27.180
I knew the world needed me to 
listen to that voice.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:35.510
Certainly the "Angel of the Crimea" was 
essential for the advancement of Earthlings.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:34.150
<b>March 31, 1888</b>

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:34.150
<b>London</b>

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:41.770
Then this year, I heard it again.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:46.620
Save me! 
Something's wrong with my body!

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.210
I am sorry.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:49.640
Truly.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:04.410
It was hard to believe 
what it was saying.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:15.670
Agent Nightingale!

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:17.980
Oh, stop.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:21.340
It's been ages since I was in 
the secret intelligence section. {TB: The Secret Intelligence Service, or even Bureau didn't exist yet, so I guess maybe it's some unofficial precursor or alternate history.}

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:27.880
It's just as you said. We found an unknown 
type of bacteria in the woman's organs.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:33.260
Scientific Advisor Dr. Moreau 
believes it may be man-made.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.470
A bacteriological weapon?

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:36.990
Yes.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:40.670
It's the worst kind of 
indiscriminate terrorism.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:44.550
If that woman's corpse had 
been abandoned in secret,

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:48.010
the bacteria might have 
raged throughout Europe.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:53.610
But why would something like 
that have been inside her?

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:58.300
Eighty percent of the people 
in that district are poor.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.590
Over half of the children there 
die before age five.

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:06.950
I wouldn't blame someone if they agreed

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:11.550
to an injection of who-knows-what

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:13.700
in exchange for some money.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:18.030
A-Anyhow, we've overcome 
the crisis now, right?

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:23.240
Wrong. There are four others 
who received the injection.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:24.340
How do you know that?!

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:29.740
You wouldn't believe me
 even if I told you.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:34.400
I will find them.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:40.420
Then you obeyed the voice, 
found the victims,

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:43.240
and collected the infected organs.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:48.510
Yes. If I listened to the voice, I could see 
the location of bacteria in the body

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:51.200
and where I should cut.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:56.370
So that's the truth behind 
the terror of London,

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.580
Jack the Ripper.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.790
But it ends today.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:09.600
She was the last one, huh.

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:13.610
We've finished burning 
the infected organs.

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:16.160
Jack the Ripper...

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.620
That handle was signed to a letter

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:22.330
sent half in jest to the police 
announcing a crime.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:27.410
But I actually think such a 
revolting name is perfectly apt.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:31.370
My sin of being unable 
to save those women

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.860
will be eternally linked 
to that name.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:40.620
I will carry it with me 
as long as I live.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:44.120
You are indeed a 
woman of distinction.

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:48.120
I'll take your power for 
this planet's future.

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:53.600
But it can't be controlled.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:07:00.560
You won't know when the person who 
inherits it will hear the voice.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:10.200
This power doesn't activate unless humanity 
is facing a critical situation, right?

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:17.190
Can't be... Is she...?

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:22.420
Well, whatever.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:25.260
Nobunagun!

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.170
Cover me for a bit!

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:28.780
Huh?!

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:33.400
Whaaaa?! Wh-What are you doing?

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:39.680
Didn't you come to save me?

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:42.800
When Nightingale Mode activates,

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:47.260
I can see the most critical place, 
where something needs saving.

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:52.960
For an enemy, 
it's their most vulnerable spot.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:56.210
In other words, their weak point.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:57.740
Found it!

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:01.090
Nobunagun, call the commander!

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:02.330
Huh?

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.340
What's going on?

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:07.550
I don't know. 
The monitor's useless.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:11.760
The last things we detected 
were the year 1888 E-gene

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.680
and the signal from ball 13.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.820
Jack the Ripper?

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:17.070
Commander!

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:20.970
Nobunagun! You're all right! 
What happened?

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:24.220
Umm, err... 
please have the tank corps

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:29.370
focus their fire on drop 
pod K6's sensor.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:30.220
What do you mean?

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:34.970
We're gonna take out the 
battleship right now!

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.860
<b>Meanwhile, in Upala</b>

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.730
Wow...

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:47.850
O-Over there!

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:53.320
It's a transport soldier 
carrying original cells!

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:57.590
Just watch. It'll be killed 
by a friendly—

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.620
Never seen one like that before!

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:05.380
It's guarding the transport soldier!

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:13.420
I see. It's just killing anything that 
gets near the transport soldier.

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:16.750
The pheromones don't figure in.

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:22.900
So what? There's just one left, right?

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:25.860
Let's do it!

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:27.230
Yeah!

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:42.920
Hold this.

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:43.700
Huh?

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:54.080
Fire!

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.180
Hold tight!

00:09:59.180 --> 00:09:59.640
Yeah!

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:25.830
Leave this to me!

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:26.160
Huh?

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:35.660
Get goin'!

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.430
Its brain should be up ahead.

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:40.320
Blow it away!

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:42.760
Roger!

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:18.020
Gaudi, keep it steady!

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:21.240
Gotcha!

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:54.060
This is it.

00:11:58.230 --> 00:11:59.980
You're up, Princess!

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:05.070
Almost died waiting!

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:08.410
Here I go!

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:39.910
Little Lady...

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:42.970
The battleship has 
ceased all activity.

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:44.960
How's Nobunagun?

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:46.710
We're confirming now.

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:10.500
U-Uh...

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:12.470
Err...

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:15.870
Recovering visuals.

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:18.080
It's...

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:21.370
It's Nobunagun and Jack the Ripper!

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:24.200
They're both fine!

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:25.920
We did it!

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:38.350
U-Uh, this is Hunter... 
Hunter from the special task force.

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:43.430
Err... mission accomplished.

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:48.330
Sio?

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:51.050
Siiio!

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:55.530
Would you like to see 
some sights together?

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:59.890
What?! Er... uh... um...

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:02.820
I guess you could say I'm not cut out 
for going around in a group.

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:07.810
But didn't you plan an operation 
and fight with everyone?

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:09.970
Yeah, but...

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:13.690
I'm kind of a class outcast, 
always by myself...

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:15.060
You're not alone.

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:16.470
Huh?

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:18.000
So, c'mon.

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:23.000
It'll be a waste 
if you don't wake up.

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:38.200
A dream?

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:51.560
Uh... Cyx?

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:55.380
Erdenebilg. Ibukigiin Erdenebilg. {TB: Worked really hard to figure out Mongol naming. Pretty sure this is right and her dad or someone's name was Ibuki. I kinda feel like it's supposed to be Erdenebile, but I guess with "gu" there, there is not much we can do?}

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:59.580
<b>Ibukigiin Erdenebilg</b>

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:56.980
You can call me "Esui."

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:59.580
<b>Esui</b>

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:59.820
Uh... okay. Esui.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:06.170
<b>Scary Esui,
 exuding Ladies gang pressure {TB: The girl version of Bousouzoku is called Ladies.}</b>

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:04.780
I... I'm sorry!

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:06.990
You're quite the gal.

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:10.030
That was an amazing operation.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:11.470
<b>Gaudi</b>

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:11.180
Uh... umm... 

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:19.770
But you know, I was stuck with two jerks 
who are not the princess riding me.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:15.890
<b>Gaudi</b>

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:17.560
<b>Gaudi</b>

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:18.930
<b>Gaudi</b>

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:24.630
You're going to take responsibility 
for robbing me of my virtue.

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:27.600
No! Hold on! It's because...

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:29.110
<b>Tongue</b>

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:29.470
Sio!

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:31.050
Miss Beckham.

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:32.510
Call me "Jess"!

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.760
Since the operation ended,

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:40.600
I've been wanting to talk to the one who 
forced such an unreasonable duty on me.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.660
<b>Holds a grudge for being given orders</b>

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:46.550
Shall we take a shower, Sio?

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:45.790
<b>Flail flail</b>

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:47.510
<b>Futile resistance</b>

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:48.970
Yeah, let's, Sio.

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:50.680
Nooo! 

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:50.680
We'll give you a good washing.

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:54.920
Looks like fun over there!

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:55.940
You think so?

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:59.760
'Cause Esui's got it where it counts.

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:00.460
What?!

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:02.890
<b>Shower room</b>

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:02.890
<b>Gaudi</b>

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:06.020
Yep, in the end we can 
only rely on analog.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.400
<b>Capa</b>

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:05.940
<b>Gandhi</b>

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.720
No peeping!

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:12.630
Wh-What?

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:18.030
Oh, there's something we haven't 
cleared up yet. Who took out the most?

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:20.190
LeMond, how many did you kill?

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:22.790
Uh... 1,002.

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:22.750
<b>LeMond: 
1,002 Objects</b>

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:24.760
Adam, how about you?

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:27.040
997.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.040
<b>Adam: 
997 Objects</b>

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:33.930
So who was the one who killed 
the other 2,000 plus, again?

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:36.550
Oh, it was me!

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:37.590
Shut up.

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:42.830
The losers have to do whatever 
the winner says, right?

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:45.310
In which case...

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:50.630
The gunboat in Sydney has gone silent. 
No other enemies detected.

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:53.240
The Fourth Platoon is repairing 
to the <i>George Atsumi</i>.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:56.170
Third Platoon, 
mission complete. We won.

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:58.810
Fifth Platoon, we're heading back.

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:01.710
Seems like it's over for now.

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:06.100
Yes. There are no longer 
any original cells.

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:10.010
They won't be able to 
reevolve anymore.

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:15.230
I'm sure that will make them frantic.

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:18.330
They'll probably get serious 
about their land invasion.

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:22.080
Give the holders a good rest.

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:24.150
Yes, of course.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:30.590
You came to visit me, Mr. Vidocq?

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:33.140
...and everybody.

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.480
But I'm happy to see you all!

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:41.070
<b>Everybody</b>

00:17:37.480 --> 00:17:41.290
During the operation I was lonely, 
'cause no one could come.

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:43.900
All of the sudden it's livened up!

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:47.580
<b>Get Well Soon 
Candied Natto </b>

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:48.120
It was hella dangerous, yo!

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:53.320
Adam and LeMond were out of energy! 
If I hadn'ta been there— Right, guys?!

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:57.340
Y-Yeah, we owe you our lives...

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:57.340
<b>We owe you...</b>

00:17:57.550 --> 00:18:03.350
<b>We'd have been dead</b>

00:17:57.730 --> 00:18:02.510
We'd have been dead 
if it weren't for Hunter.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:03.500
Princess...

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:05.700
Right? That's how it was!

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:09.830
And then, ya know, that 
pheromone extraction, man! 

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:11.600
Would've been a fine feat if he 
weren't bragging so much.

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:13.260
Just a flash of genius, I'm tellin' ya. 

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:13.260
Umm...

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:16.220
I'm still convalescing,

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:16.690
<b>Convalescing</b>

00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:20.260
so my being unable to 
handle all your bragging

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:18.950
<b>Bragging</b>

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:20.610
<b>Can't handle it</b>

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:24.700
might show on my face... 
But that won't bother you, right?

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:27.390
Oh, no problem, no problem!

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:29.070
Wait.

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:30.350
Ha.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:36.470
It's all thanks to you straining yourself 
to get the original cell data for us...

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:38.220
...Galiko.

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:42.200
Oh, I'm so happy 
I could be of service!

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:45.120
Ahh, owowow! 
A tear got in my wound.

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:43.100
<b>Four months for complete recovery</b>

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:46.250
Just relax.

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:48.750
Sorry, Mr. Vidocq.

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:49.780
Just relax.

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:55.080
What?!

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:58.610
But what an amazing operation!

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:03.350
Of course the holder teams, but thinking 
to use tanks and drop pods—

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:05.540
I'd expect nothing less from Mr. Vidocq!

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:07.640
Huh?

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:09.890
Um...

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:10.730
<b>No one can save her.</b>

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:12.760
Err...

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:19.290
Can I borrow you for a sec?

00:19:22.190 --> 00:19:24.790
So? What did you wanna talk about?

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:27.990
When we were fighting the battleship...

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:33.810
Oh, that. Thanks for 
not telling the commander.

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:34.940
Huh?

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:41.070
It'd be a whole thing if Jack the 
Ripper's true identity got out.

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:46.100
The only ones who know right now are me,
 you, and the Dogoo alien.

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:47.440
Yeah, but I don't mean that...

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:49.000
Hm?

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:52.620
Well... just...

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:54.170
What?

00:19:55.190 --> 00:20:00.220
I was gonna thank you for 
coming to rescue me, but...

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:03.980
Then you said <i>you</i> were 
 thanking <i>me</i>, so...

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:06.600
Well...

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:09.680
...you're just so important.

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:19.270
I heard my E-gene's voice 
telling me to save you.

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:19.850
Huh?

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:27.540
That voice supposedly doesn't speak except 
at critical junctures for this planet.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:32.840
You sure don't look it, but apparently 
you're valuable to this world.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:39.570
Ah... that's it. 
Well, that makes sense...

00:20:40.390 --> 00:20:43.900
I just did what it said. 
Don't dwell on it.

00:20:44.310 --> 00:20:46.320
I was kinda stoked.

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:49.750
'Cause this is me... yeah.

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:53.190
To this planet, huh.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:56.260
Not to you personally or anything...

00:20:56.750 --> 00:21:00.410
Ha... what was I thinking?

00:21:01.100 --> 00:21:04.860
I was... so happy.

00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:10.160
Oh, by the way, Sio. 
You know...

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:12.070
Hm?

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:38.600
That just now... 
wasn't on my E-gene's orders.

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:48.710
